  "description": "Core abstractions and engine for DotNetBoost.Auditing — who changed what, when, and from\n      what to what, for any entity in the application, in two tables with no column on your\n      entities. Includes IAuditManager (the one service application code injects), the store\n      contract (IAuditStore), IAuditObserver for finding out what was deliberately not recorded,\n      plus the store-neutral recording path: entity addressing, actor capture, correlation,\n      per-type ignore and redaction rules, and value truncation. Depends on no other DotNetBoost\n      package, and on one NuGet package in total.",
